    "body": "Claim released. STOPPED after the required quick gate failed and its failing test failed again.\n\nThe zero-dwell bug reproduces. grblhal_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0 and tormach_zero_dwell_g86_has_p0 both fail before the fix because G86 has no P0. Both pass with the two post conditions changed. All nine bore_cycle tests pass.\n\nEach post was replaced with upstream/main's version for a separate mutation check. Its pin failed. Restoring the fixed post made its pin pass.\n\nThe quick gate ran 588 steps. One failed: microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a. The wrapped-A golden differs at line 2477: F138.835 versus F138.781, beyond the 0.04 allowance. The exact test fails again. It also fails identically with both original posts restored from parent PR #2342. This failure is inherited and unrelated to G86. No unrelated golden was updated. Clippy was not run after the stop condition.\n\nOverlap check found onCycle in PR #2342. This branch stacks one level on its head f29c92bd1. PRs #2346 and #2386 inherit that change. No PR was opened and nothing was pushed.\n\nThe held patch is in /Users/mikekinney/CamcraftPool/.claude/worktrees/issue-2362 on issue/2362-g86-zero-dwell. It changes two post conditions, the bore pins, and two bore goldens with P0 only. The fixed posts are restored. Logs remain local, outside the patch.\n",
